    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-University-Researcher-in-Intellectual-History/1371301457/?feedId=350602&utm_source=CareerSite_UniversityOfHelsinki": {
      "title": "University Researcher in Intellectual History",
      "description": "University Researcher in Intellectual History Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University Researcher in Intellectual History The Centre of Excellence in Meliorist Philosophy of Suffering (MePhiS) , funded by the Research Council of Finland at the University of Helsinki and Tampere University, invites applications for a fixed-term University Researcher position in Intellectual History. University Researcher position is open within MePhiS’s research team History of Ethics and Law of Responding to Suffering hosted by the Faculty of Theology at the University of Helsinki City Centre Campus. The position is fixed-term (two years) starting in January 2027 or earlier/later as agreed. MePhiS engages in philosophical and interdisciplinary scholarship that places the concept of suffering at the centre of philosophical reflection and offers conceptual and argumentative tools for a deeper understanding of human engagement with affliction, starting from the meliorist (Lat. melior , better) idea that the world can and should be made better through active human efforts. According to meliorism, a positive outcome is neither guaranteed (optimism) nor impossible (pessimism). The team History of Ethics and Law of Responding to Suffering investigates how medieval and early modern thinkers conceptualised and responded to extreme human and non-human suffering in Western history, with particular attention to proposed ethical and practical means of alleviating it. The team further explores how these historical responses to extremes can reflect the meliorist stance to suffering. The University Researcher will be responsible for researching the ethics of suffering and meliorism in intellectual history; analysing ethical, legal, moral-theological, and/or political responses to suffering; authoring scholarly publications on the research topic; collaborating with other members of the Centre of Excellence, including through joint publications and other research activities; and contributing to teaching and administrative duties, amounting to approximately 5–10 % of the working time. Requirements for the position and assessment of qualifications We seek candidates with expertise in intellectual history who are interested in advancing the research aims described above. Applicants must hold a doctoral degree in a relevant field within the humanities or social sciences and have demonstrated track record of high-quality research and international publications. We are looking for a senior researcher with a background in intellectual history, specializing in medieval or early modern period. A pre-existing interest in the general theme of the CoE is an advantage. A University Researcher typically has at least ca. five years of postdoctoral experience. In addition, applicants should possess ability to lead a research group, a track record of securing external funding, and the teaching skills required to successfully perform the duties and responsibilities of the position. The selected candidate should be capable of conducting independent research at a high international level and able to work both independently and collaboratively as a member of the research team. The working language of MePhiS is English, and excellent written and oral communication skills in English are required. Applicants should be prepared to provide proof of their qualifications upon request. Please do not submit AI-generated proposals. What we offer The position is fixed term for one or two years starting in January 2027 or earlier/later as agreed. A six-month trial period applies to new employees at University of Helsinki. The salary will be based on the University Salary System. The salary of a University Researcher is at levels 6–7. In addition to the basic salary, a performance-based salary component is paid according to the appointee’s qualifications and experience. The appointee will be paid a salary component based on personal performance. The annual gross salary is €51,000 - €59,000. The appointee is expected to reside in Finland while employed by the University of Helsinki. The university is an internationally renowned research university offering a wide range of staff benefits, including occupational health care and health insurance, flexible working hours, excellent campus sports facilities, and opportunities for professional development. The University provides support for internationally recruited employees with their transition to work and life in Finland. More information here. The Faculty of Theology is well-known for its internationally acknowledged research in the fields represented by MePhiS, and there are close ties with the Faculty of Humanities, the Faculty of Law, the Faculty of Social Science, and the Faculty of Education, as well as other units on the City Centre Campus. The University of Helsinki welcomes applicants from a variety of genders, linguistic and cultural backgrounds, and minorities. A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. For more information about Helsinki, please see My Helsinki. For further information about Finland, please visit infoFinland and This is Finland . How to apply Applications must be submitted in English through the University of Helsinki electronic recruitment system (link below). Current employees of the University of Helsinki must submit their applications through SAP Fiori’s Suffeli recruitment portal. The closing date for applications is 30 September 2026 (at 23:56/UTC+3). The online interviews to shortlisted candidates will be announced later. The following documents must be attached to your application: CV (max. 3 pages, including contact details of two referees) A list of publications A letter of motivation (max. 1 page) outlining your motivation for applying, relevant expertise, and how you would contribute to the research aims and collaborative activities of the project. A research proposal (max. 3 pages) consisting of a description of how your previous research experience and current work align with the overarching aims of the team; a research idea outlining why the project’s themes or approach interest you and how you position your own research within this context; a preliminary publication plan. Enquiries For further information about the position please contact the project PI, Senior University Lecturer Virpi Mäkinen, virpi.makinen(at)helsinki.fi. For questions regarding the application process, please contact recruitment(at)helsinki.fi (please indicate in the heading which position you are inquiring about). JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 30.9.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Theology Sub-unit: Faculty of Theology ID: 5200 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Teaching and research positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management system for conversion tracking, site analytics, remarketing and more. Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleTagManager Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleAnalytics LinkedIn LinkedIn is an employment-oriented social networking service. We use the Apply with LinkedIn feature to allow you to apply for jobs using your LinkedIn profile. Opting out of LinkedIn cookies will disable your ability to use Apply with LinkedIn. Cookie Policy Cookie Table Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider LinkedIn Confirm 