    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Ecological-Networks-and-Biodiversity-Conservation/1370769357/?feedId=350602&utm_source=CareerSite_UniversityOfHelsinki": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Ecological Networks and Biodiversity Conservation",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Ecological Networks and Biodiversity Conservation Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoctoral Researcher in Ecological Networks and Biodiversity Conservation Postdoctoral Researcher in Ecological Networks and Biodiversity Conservation The Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences at the University of Helsinki invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position in ecological networks and biodiversity conservation. The work will be based at the Viikki Campus in Helsinki, Finland. The postdoctoral researcher will join the research project ANEW – Arising Novelty in Ecological Networks: consequences for ecosystem functioning and biodiversity conservation , funded by the Research Council of Finland and Emil Aaltonen Foundation, and work under the supervision of Academy Researcher Emma-Liina Marjakangas. ANEW aims to understand how novel ecological interactions emerge under global change, how they affect ecosystem functioning, and how this knowledge can improve conservation of species interactions. The ANEW team consists of the PI, a postdoctoral researcher, a doctoral researcher, and a research assistant. The project also involves collaboration with Professors Heini Kujala (University of Helsinki, Finland) and Matthias Schleuning (Senckenberg Biodiversity and Climate Research Centre, Germany). Together, the team combines expertise in ecological networks, spatial ecology, conservation science, and biodiversity informatics. The position is funded for 24 months and is available from 1st January 2027 , or as agreed. About the position Understanding how ecosystems respond to global change is one of the central challenges in ecology. This postdoctoral project investigates how ecological novelty influences ecosystem functioning and the ecological and environmental processes driving the emergence of novel interactions. The successful candidate will contribute to advancing ecological network theory while developing a mechanistic understanding of how changing species interactions influence biodiversity and ecosystem functioning. The postdoctoral researcher will play a leading scientific role within ANEW. They will lead research on the mechanisms underlying ecological network novelty and its consequences for ecosystem functioning by combining large-scale ecological datasets, species trait data, ecological network analyses, and quantitative modelling. The postdoctoral researcher will also coordinate and lead field resurveys of historical seed dispersal networks in Finland and other European countries and contribute to planning and implementing international field campaigns. Beyond their own research, the postdoctoral researcher will have an active role in shaping the scientific direction of the project by mentoring the doctoral researcher and research assistant and leading collaborative scientific publications. The position therefore offers excellent opportunities to gain leadership experience while building an independent research profile. The Postdoctoral Researcher will also have opportunities to collaborate with international researchers and present research at international conferences. Selection criteria We are looking for a highly motivated and collaborative researcher with a strong background in ecology and quantitative analyses, who is excited to contribute to an ambitious international research project. The successful applicant must have: •    A PhD (completed before the start of employment) in ecology, evolutionary biology, conservation biology, biology, environmental sciences, or another relevant field •    Strong quantitative and analytical skills, including experience handling and analyzing ecological or environmental data (in R) •    Research experience in ecological networks, community ecology, functional ecology, biodiversity conservation, global change ecology, or another closely related research area •    Experience in conducting ecological fieldwork, including bird and/or plant identification skills •    A record of publishing peer-reviewed scientific research appropriate to career stage •    Excellent written and spoken communication skills in English The following qualifications are considered an advantage: •    Experience working with large biodiversity datasets •    Experience with seed dispersal ecology, plant-animal interactions, species traits, or ecosystem functioning •    Experience coordinating collaborative research projects or field campaigns •    The ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative and interdisciplinary research team We recognize that excellent candidates may not meet every preferred qualification. If your experience matches the essential requirements and you are enthusiastic about the project, we strongly encourage you to apply. Why work for us? This position offers an exciting opportunity to play a central scientific role in a newly funded research project addressing fundamental questions about how ecological interactions respond to global environmental change. As the project's postdoctoral researcher, you will help shape the scientific direction of ANEW from an early stage. You will lead field campaigns, coordinate collaborative publications, and mentor junior researchers. The position therefore provides hands-on experience in scientific leadership, project coordination, supervision, and international collaboration. You will join the ANEW research team at the University of Helsinki and collaborate closely with researchers at the University of Helsinki and the Senckenberg Biodiversity and Climate Research Centre in Germany. The project includes international collaborations, opportunities to present research at international conferences, and fieldwork in Finland and elsewhere in Europe. The Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences is an internationally recognized research environment with strong expertise in ecology, evolution, conservation biology, and environmental sciences. Located on the Viikki Campus, it provides excellent research infrastructure and a vibrant international scientific community. The University of Helsinki supports researchers through extensive training opportunities, language courses, and career development services. Salary and working hours The position is funded for 24 months . The working hours will be 1612 hours on a yearly basis under the annual workload scheme for research and teaching staff. The gross monthly salary is based on the salary system of Finnish universities according to the job requirement level for postdoctoral researchers (approximately €3700–€4200/month ), depending on the appointee's qualifications and experience. Further information about staff benefits is available on University of Helsinki website . The postdoctoral researcher should reside in Finland while employed by the University of Helsinki. The University assists employees from abroad with their transition to work and life in Finland. Finland is a member of the European Union, has high quality free schooling (also in English), generous family benefits and healthcare. Helsinki offers an outstanding quality of life, and Finland is consistently ranked among the world's best countries for safety, work-life balance, education, and family-friendliness. The University of Helsinki offers comprehensive occupational health care, flexible working hours, excellent sports facilities, staff training opportunities, and support for international employees relocating to Finland. Read more about why the University of Helsinki is an excellent career choice: working at the University of Helsinki and living in Finland . How to apply Applications must be submitted through the University of Helsinki electronic recruitment system by clicking on the link below. Current employees of the University of Helsinki must submit their applications through SAP Fiori’s Suffeli recruitment portal. Please submit your application through the University of Helsinki electronic recruitment system via the Apply Now button no later than the end of 30th September 2026 (23:59 Helsinki time). Your application should include the following documents written in English as a single PDF called \" lastname_firstname \": 1.    A motivation letter (maximum one page) describing your research interests, relevant experience, and motivation for applying for the position 2.    A curriculum vitae 3.    A list of publications, including manuscripts in preparation 4.    A copy of your PhD certificate (or documentation confirming that the degree will be completed before the start of employment) 5.    The names and contact details of two referees Further information about the position can be obtained from Academy Research Fellow Emma-Liina Marjakangas ( emma.marjakangas@helsinki.fi ). Support with the recruitment system can be obtained from University of Helsinki HR Specialists at recruitment@helsinki.fi . A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 30.9.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Sub-unit: Department of Organismal and Evolutionary Biology ID: 5181 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Teaching and research positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management system for conversion tracking, site analytics, remarketing and more. Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleTagManager Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports websi